obs The page then read C+ 76 at Door and B 84 at Field -- the same bytes, eight points apart. That is the exact question I put on the card last lap, now carrying a price: whether a module reference README is Door or Field is worth eight points on this one page, and its own Status line reads Checkable. Left it repaired and unrostered until the word comes; it drops off the candidate list either way, since the candidate list reads pages over the ceiling.
obs CLAIM_PRESERVE_FILES=... sh tools/fixtures/c/claim_preserve_scan.sh reported four FAILs across the pair, every one on the modality axis: never 6 to 5 and 2 to 1, all 1 to 2, every 6 to 7. Removing a negation is what a register molt does, so the modality counter reads the sanctioned repair as drift. Each of the four was read by hand and holds its claim -- leaks nothing it was never told to keep became holds exactly what it was told to keep, and never its execution floor became RISC-V through Zig is its execution floor. Named on the card rather than booked, since construction/REDS.md closes at 10 bytes free with every row OPEN.
obs My own cold pass went void and the fault was mine: I edited three files while it ran, which is the one thing the card asks a lap not to do, so its open and close digests differ and its verdict is tree_moved. The hot pass after git add is this lap's pass of record. Patchouli booked this same shape at 20260910.043900 and I repeated it.
